7) Forms you’ll likely use (federal)
- Form 1040 (main return)
- Schedule 1 (additional income and adjustments: student loan interest, deductible part of SE tax, etc.)
- Schedule C (Profit or Loss from Business) — for the $11,200 web‑design income and related expenses
- Form 8829 (Expenses for Business Use of Your Home) — if you use the actual expense method for the home office
- Schedule SE (Self‑Employment Tax)
- Form 8995 or 8995‑A (Qualified Business Income deduction), if applicable
- Schedule A only if you decide to itemize (unlikely based on numbers you’ve given)
- Any 1099‑INT / 1099‑DIV / 1099‑B attachments or statements as required
- Oregon state return (OR‑40) — Oregon filing forms (and any local schedules) as required

