- Based on rent $2,400/month, the actual method (≈$4,744 rent share) is far larger than the simplified $700. As long as your home office meets the exclusive & regular use test and your allocated expenses don’t exceed your net business income limit, the actual method will likely yield a larger deduction.
- If you use the actual method for a self‑employed person you generally fill out Form 8829 (Expenses for Business Use of Your Home) to compute allowable home office deduction (then transfer to Schedule C). If you use simplified, record the $5 × sq ft on Schedule C and you do not file Form 8829.

Forms you’ll likely need (federal)
