- Schedule C (Profit or Loss From Business) — report web-design income and business expenses (including home office expense if using simplified method, you report the simplified home office deduction on Schedule C line 30, box to check for simplified; actual method uses Form 8829)
- Schedule SE (Self-Employment Tax) — calculate SE tax and half-SE adjustment
- Form 8995 (Qualified Business Income Deduction simplified form) if you claim QBI (or Form 8995-A if you need full calculation)
- Form 1098-E (student loan interest statement) — use to support the student loan interest deduction (you should receive this from FedLoan)
- Form(s) 1099-NEC or 1099-MISC if you received them from clients (gives proof of self-employment income)
- Forms 1099-INT (interest statements) for the Goldman and TD Ameritrade interest (for your records and Form 1040 reporting)
- Schedule A (Itemized Deductions) only if you choose to itemize (unlikely here)
- State: Oregon Form OR-40 (resident) — Oregon tax return uses federal AGI as a starting point; check Oregon-specific additions or subtractions. Oregon may have different rules for deductions/credits.

